{title: Eternal Father, Strong to Save}
{artist: William Whiting / John B. Dykes}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: C}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Book of Hymns (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1966), # 538)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Eternal Father, [F]strong to [C]save,
[C]Whose [Am]arm__[D]__ hath [G]bound the [D]restless [G7]wave,
[G7]Who bidd’st the [C]mighty [A7]ocean [D]deep
[D]Its [Em]own appointed [B]limits [Em]keep;
[Em]Oh, [C7]hear us [F]when we [D7]cry to [G7]Thee,
[G7]For [C]those in per[G7]il on the [C]sea!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]O Christ! Whose voice the [F]waters [C]heard
[C]And [Am]hushed__[D]__ their [G]raging [D]at Thy [G7]Word,
[G7]Who walked up[C]on the [A7]foaming [D]deep,
[D]And [Em]calm amidst its [B]rage didst [Em]sleep;
[Em]Oh, [C7]hear us [F]when we [D7]cry to [G7]Thee,
[G7]For [C]those in per[G7]il on the [C]sea!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Most Holy Spirit! [F]Who didst [C]brood
[C]Up[Am]on__[D]__ the [G]chaos [D]dark and [G7]rude,
[G7]And bid its [C]angry [A7]tumult [D]cease,
[D]And [Em]give, for wild con[B]fusion, [Em]peace;
[Em]Oh, [C7]hear us [F]when we [D7]cry to [G7]Thee,
[G7]For [C]those in per[G7]il on the [C]sea!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]O Trinity of [F]love and [C]power!
[C]Our [Am]fam__[D]__ily [G]shield in [D]danger’s [G7]hour;
[G7]From rock and [C]tempest, [A7]fire and [D]foe,
[D]Pro[Em]tect us whereso[B]e’er we [Em]go;
[Em]Thus [C7]ever[F]more shall [D7]rise to [G7]Thee
[G7]Glad [C]hymns of praise [G7]from land and [C]sea.
{end_of_verse}
